.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt YKURCTRL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ykurctrl
.Nd switch the relay and ports of a Yepkit YKUR board over USB HID
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -no-wait
.Op Fl s Ar SERIAL
.Fl u Ar PORT
.Nm
.Op Fl -no-wait
.Op Fl s Ar SERIAL
.Fl d Ar PORT
.Nm
.Op Fl -no-wait
.Op Fl s Ar SERIAL
.Fl g Ar PORT
.Nm
.Op Fl -no-wait
.Op Fl s Ar SERIAL
.Fl v
.Nm
.Fl l
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
switches the on-board relay and the four relay driver ports of a Yepkit YKUR
USB relay board (VID 0x04D8, PID 0xF1CB) and reads back their state.
Every switching command is confirmed by reading the state back; a target that
did not switch is reported as an error.
.Pp
Two invocations addressing the same board take turns: on Linux through an
advisory
.Xr flock 2
on the board's
.Pa /dev/hidrawN
node, on FreeBSD through the single-open
.Xr hidraw 4
node itself, and on macOS through an exclusive IOKit open.
A second invocation waits up to five seconds for the board, or fails at once
with
.Fl -no-wait .
.Pp
.Fl -no-wait
and
.Fl s
go before the command, in either order, each at most once.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-s SERIAL"
.It Fl u Ar PORT
Switch
.Ar PORT
on and confirm the state by reading it back.
.It Fl d Ar PORT
Switch
.Ar PORT
off and confirm the state by reading it back.
.It Fl g Ar PORT
Print whether
.Ar PORT
is on or off, one line per output, as in
.Ql Port 1: on
or
.Ql Relay: off .
.It Fl v
Print the firmware version of the board.
.It Fl l
List the serial numbers of the attached YKUR boards.
.It Fl s Ar SERIAL
Address the board with serial number
.Ar SERIAL
instead of the first one the system enumerates.
.It Fl -no-wait
Fail at once with exit status 75 when the board is in use, instead of waiting
up to five seconds for it.
.It Fl -version
Print the version of
.Nm .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage summary.
.El
.Pp
.Ar PORT
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width "everything" -compact
.It Cm 1 .. Cm 4
One of the four relay driver ports.
.It Cm r
The on-board relay.
.It Cm a
All four relay driver ports at once; the relay is left alone.
.It Cm everything
All four relay driver ports and the on-board relay at once.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status follows
.Xr sysexits 3 :
.Bl -tag -width "101" -compact
.It Cm 0
Success; also
.Fl l
when no board is attached, and when the reader of standard output closed the
pipe early.
.It Cm 64
Invalid command line.
.It Cm 69
No board found, unknown serial number, board disconnected, or the board
reported an error.
.It Cm 74
No answer within the five second timeout, a truncated report, a transport
error, or writing to standard output failed for another reason than a closed
pipe.
.It Cm 75
The board is in use by another process (after waiting five seconds, or at once
with
.Fl -no-wait ) .
.It Cm 76
An answer from the board did not fit the request.
.It Cm 77
Permission denied opening the device node.
.It Cm 101
Internal panic.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Switch relay driver port 1 on, read all outputs including the relay, and switch
everything off on board
.Ql YK22170 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ykurctrl -u 1
ykurctrl -g everything
ykurctrl -s YK22170 -d everything
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr flock 2 ,
.Xr sysexits 3
